WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.040
Parents, families, friends, 

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.670
welcome to the 309th commencement

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.860
of Yale University.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:02.200
We gather to recognize the extraordinary accomplishments
of all you who have worked so hard

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.120
to complete your programs of study.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.560
We salute your effort,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.920
your diligence,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.820
your talent, and your intellect.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:16.320
We also join you in expressing gratitude for
all who have supported you in these endeavors:

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.710
your families,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.009
friends, teachers,

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:21.799
and other members of the Yale community.

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:25.750
In keeping with the tradition of this occasion,
I now call upon the chaplain

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:32.750
to offer an invocation.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.300
My sisters and my brothers,

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.880
let us pray.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.740
Almighty God,

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.890
source of all truth,

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.760
here we stand in the splendor of 

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.310
this morning, many expressions of one living mystery,

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.660
which is beyond all telling.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.579
As students of your handiwork,

00:01:56.579 --> 00:01:59.850
we have gathered from all parts of your world

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.430
with exquisite ambitions

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.730
and have been blessed at this place of truth
and light

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:10.639
with the freedom to let them grow.

00:02:10.639 --> 00:02:13.159
You walk with us when we stumble

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:15.119
and when we sore.

00:02:15.119 --> 00:02:18.909
As we pause here, embraced by this moment,

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:23.290
we are grateful for our beloved families and
friends,

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.959
yet we are mindful of the dear ones

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:30.709
who are not here and they are deeply missed.

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:33.439
Our God of all generations,

00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:34.879
you are the guardian

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:36.510
of where we are going

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.849
and who we are becoming.

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:44.659
You have called us to lovingly shape this beautiful yet aching world.

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:45.930
We are humbled, 

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.180
but ready.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.279
Now we ask you,

00:02:49.279 --> 00:02:53.159
bless our hands with tenderness for all that we touch,

00:02:53.159 --> 00:02:58.569
bless our lips with wise words so we speak in healing ways,

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:03.999
bless our eyes with an impassioned vision
so we are never blind to 

00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:05.709
possibility, and bless our hearing

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:09.979
so we may be open to all understanding.

00:03:09.979 --> 00:03:12.559
From this moment on,

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:16.399
infuse our hearts with an imaginative daring,

00:03:16.399 --> 00:03:19.099
one that stirs us to become

00:03:19.099 --> 00:03:20.549
living,

00:03:20.549 --> 00:03:22.159
vibrant examples

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:23.509
of 

00:03:23.509 --> 00:03:25.179
shalom, of salaam, 

00:03:25.179 --> 00:03:26.659
of shanti,

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:28.260
of peace.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.949
For this we say.

00:03:29.949 --> 00:03:36.949
amen. 

